---
title: Row & Column Management
---
sequenceDiagram
    actor User
    participant BoardMenu as BoardMenu / BoardDock<br/>(BoardMenu.tsx #board-menu = lg+,<br/>BoardDock.tsx dock = below lg)
    participant Config as BoardConfigModal<br/>(BoardConfigModal.tsx +<br/>config/board/*Section.tsx.<br/>Column drag-to-reorder scaffolding lives in<br/>config/board/ColumnReorderList.tsx, shared with<br/>the homepage DemoExperience demo)
    participant RowModal as CreateRowModal<br/>(config/board/CreateRowModal.tsx +<br/>CreateRowSection.tsx)
    participant Board as RowBoard<br/>(RowBoard.tsx)
    participant Row as RowSection<br/>(RowSection.tsx)
    participant Cell as ColumnSection<br/>(ColumnSection.tsx)
    participant Actions as action hooks<br/>(actions/boardConfig.ts,<br/>row*.ts, column*.ts, view.ts)
    participant Reducer as reducers<br/>(board.ts, rows.ts, columns.ts, taskAi.ts, view.ts)
    participant Ctx as BoardContext<br/>(BoardConfig/BoardData/RowForm/<br/>RowEdit/ColumnEdit/ColumnConfig/ColumnFilter)
    participant AI as /api/generate-tasks<br/>(Google GenAI)

    Note over User,AI: Open board configuration modal<br/>(gear icon, or "Add new column to all rows" menu item)
    alt gear icon
        User->>BoardMenu: click gear (#board-config-collapse-toggle)
        BoardMenu->>Actions: openBoardConfigModal()<br/>(actions/boardConfig.ts)
    else "Add new column to all rows" menu item
        User->>BoardMenu: click "Add new column to all rows"
        BoardMenu->>Actions: openBoardConfigModal("create-new-column")
    end
    Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(BOARD_CONFIG/OPEN_MODAL, {scrollTarget?})
    Ctx->>Reducer: board.openConfigModal
    Reducer-->>Ctx: boardConfigModalOpen = true<br/>boardConfigScrollTarget = scrollTarget ?? null
    Ctx-->>Config: BoardConfigModal re-renders<br/>(BoardConfigContext: boardConfigModalOpen=true)<br/>-> modal opens, sections below become visible
    opt boardConfigScrollTarget set
        Config->>Config: useEffect[open, scrollTarget]<br/>-> requestAnimationFrame<br/>-> getElementById(scrollTarget).scrollIntoView({block:"start"})<br/>(scrolls to #create-new-column in ColumnSettingsSection)
    end

    Note over Board,RowModal: CreateRowSection also renders inline in RowBoard's<br/>empty state (rows.length === 0), not only inside CreateRowModal.
    Note over User,AI: Open / close the Add-row modal (CreateRowModal)
    User->>BoardMenu: click "Add new project row"
    BoardMenu->>Actions: openCreateRowModal()<br/>(actions/rowForm.ts)
    Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(ROW/OPEN_CREATE_MODAL)
    Ctx->>Reducer: rows.openRowCreateModal
    Reducer-->>Ctx: createRowModalOpen = true
    Ctx-->>RowModal: CreateRowModal re-renders<br/>(RowFormContext: createRowModalOpen=true)<br/>-> modal opens, CreateRowSection visible
    Note over RowModal: Close (X / backdrop) -> closeCreateRowModal()<br/>-> ROW/CLOSE_CREATE_MODAL -> rows.closeRowCreateModal<br/>-> createRowModalOpen=false,<br/>taskGenerationStatus="", taskGenerationFailed=false

    Note over User,AI: Add row with AI task generation<br/>(CreateRowSection, inside CreateRowModal)
    User->>RowModal: type row name + AI prompt
    RowModal->>Actions: setNewRowName / setNewRowPrompt<br/>(actions/rowForm.ts)
    Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(ROW/SET_NEW_NAME | ROW/SET_NEW_PROMPT)
    Ctx->>Reducer: rows.setNewName / setNewPrompt
    Reducer-->>Ctx: newRowName / newRowPrompt updated
    Ctx-->>RowModal: CreateRowModal re-renders<br/>(RowFormContext: newRowName/newRowPrompt changed)

    User->>RowModal: submit "Add row" form
    RowModal->>Actions: addRow(event)<br/>(actions/rowForm.ts)<br/>builds newRow = {id, title, color: blue, order}

    alt newRowPrompt is non-empty
        Note over Actions: generateTasksForRow(newRow) — the row is only<br/>created once tasks come back, so the modal stays open
        Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(TASK_AI/GENERATE_START)
        Ctx->>Reducer: taskAi.generateStart
        Reducer-->>Ctx: isGeneratingTasks = true, taskGenerationFailed = false<br/>taskGenerationStatus = "Generating tasks..."
        Ctx-->>RowModal: CreateRowModal re-renders<br/>(RowFormContext: isGeneratingTasks=true)<br/>-> modal stays open, GeneratingTasksAlert (info),<br/>inputs disabled, Add Row hidden

        Actions->>AI: fetchGeneratedItems(prompt, 10)<br/>(actions/shared.ts)<br/>POST /api/generate-tasks
        AI-->>Actions: {response: string[]} (task titles)

        alt titles returned
            Actions->>Actions: buildTasksFromTitles(titles, newRow.id, columns)<br/>(todoColId = findTodoColumnId(columns),<br/>orders = generateNKeysBetween(null, null, n))
            Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(ROW/ADD, newRow)
            Ctx->>Reducer: rows.add(state, payload)
            Reducer-->>Ctx: rows = [...rows, newRow]
            Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(TASK_AI/GENERATE_SUCCESS, {tasks})
            Ctx->>Reducer: taskAi.generateSuccess
            Reducer-->>Ctx: tasks = [...newTasks, ...tasks]<br/>isGeneratingTasks=false, taskGenerationFailed=false<br/>taskGenerationStatus = "Added N task(s) to first column."<br/>newRowName="", newRowPrompt="", newRowFormKey++
            Ctx-->>RowModal: CreateRowModal re-renders<br/>-> form resets, GeneratingTasksAlert (success, green)<br/>shows the completion status
            Ctx-->>Config: BoardConfigModal re-renders<br/>(BoardData: rows changed)<br/>-> row settings list shows new row
            Ctx-->>Row: RowBoard mounts a new RowSection<br/>(BoardData: rows changed)<br/>-> isNew=true (id not in RowBoard seenRowIds ref)
            Row->>Row: useEffect -> animejs createScope + splitText(title, chars)<br/>+ animate(chars, {y bounce, rotate from -1turn, stagger(50),<br/>autoplay: onScroll({repeat:false})})<br/>-> title chars jump/spin in once when scrolled into view.<br/>RowBoard then marks the id seen, so remounts (e.g. column<br/>filter toggles) never replay it
            Ctx-->>Cell: ColumnSection (Todo column, new row)<br/>re-renders (TasksByCellContext changed)<br/>-> new TaskCards mount
            Actions->>Actions: await 3000ms (CLOSE_AFTER_GENERATE_MS)
            Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(ROW/CLOSE_CREATE_MODAL)<br/>then scrollToRow -> requestAnimationFrame -><br/>getElementById("row-section-{id}").scrollIntoView({behavior:"smooth", block:"start"})
            Ctx->>Reducer: rows.closeRowCreateModal
            Reducer-->>Ctx: createRowModalOpen = false<br/>taskGenerationStatus = "", taskGenerationFailed = false
            Ctx-->>RowModal: CreateRowModal re-renders<br/>-> modal closes, window scrolls to the new RowSection
        else no titles / fetch error
            Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(TASK_AI/GENERATE_FAILURE, {error})
            Ctx->>Reducer: taskAi.generateFailure
            Reducer-->>Ctx: isGeneratingTasks=false, taskGenerationFailed=true<br/>taskGenerationStatus=error<br/>(newRowName/newRowPrompt kept; no ROW/ADD)
            Ctx-->>RowModal: CreateRowModal re-renders<br/>-> modal stays open, GeneratingTasksAlert (error),<br/>inputs re-enabled, Add Row reappears for retry
        end
        Note over Board,RowModal: In RowBoard's inline empty state there is no modal:<br/>ROW/ADD swaps the empty state for the board, and the<br/>delayed ROW/CLOSE_CREATE_MODAL is a no-op.
    else newRowPrompt empty
        Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(ROW/ADD, newRow)
        Ctx->>Reducer: rows.add(state, payload)
        Reducer-->>Ctx: rows = [...rows, newRow]
        Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(ROW/CLOSE_CREATE_MODAL)<br/>then scrollToRow -> requestAnimationFrame -><br/>getElementById("row-section-{id}").scrollIntoView({behavior:"smooth", block:"start"})
        Ctx->>Reducer: rows.closeRowCreateModal
        Reducer-->>Ctx: createRowModalOpen = false<br/>taskGenerationStatus = "", taskGenerationFailed = false
        Ctx-->>RowModal: CreateRowModal re-renders<br/>(RowFormContext: createRowModalOpen=false)<br/>-> modal closes, window scrolls to the new RowSection
        Ctx-->>Config: BoardConfigModal re-renders<br/>(BoardData: rows changed)<br/>-> row settings list shows new row
        Ctx-->>Row: RowBoard mounts a new RowSection<br/>(BoardData: rows changed)<br/>-> isNew=true, title entrance animation (as above)
        Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(ROW/RESET_FORM)
        Ctx->>Reducer: rows.resetForm
        Reducer-->>Ctx: newRowName="", newRowPrompt="", newRowFormKey++
        Ctx-->>RowModal: CreateRowModal re-renders<br/>(RowFormContext: form fields reset)
    end

    Note over User,AI: Create task from board menu (TaskCreateModal)
    Note over BoardMenu: "Create new task" is only in addActions<br/>when rows.length > 0 (useSharedMenuActions)
    User->>BoardMenu: click "Create new task"
    BoardMenu->>Actions: openTaskForm("", "")<br/>(actions/task.ts)
    Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(TASK/OPEN_CREATE_MODAL, {rowId:"", colId:""})
    Ctx->>Reducer: tasks.openCreateModal
    Reducer-->>Ctx: taskCreateModalOpen=true<br/>taskDraft=emptyTaskDraft("", "")
    Note over BoardMenu: TaskCreateModal opens with empty, required<br/>Status (colId) + Row (rowId) selects.<br/>createTask gates on form checkValidity() -> submit blocked<br/>until both are chosen, so no orphan (rowId/colId="") task.

    Note over User,AI: Rename row (RowSection)
    User->>Row: double-click row title
    Row->>Actions: editRowTitle(row)<br/>(actions/rowEdit.ts)
    Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(ROW/EDIT_START, {rowId, currentName})
    Ctx->>Reducer: rows.editStart
    Reducer-->>Ctx: editingRowId = rowId, editingRowName = currentName
    Ctx-->>Row: every RowSection re-renders<br/>(RowEditContext: editingRowId changed)<br/>-> matching row shows input, others unchanged

    User->>Row: type new name
    Row->>Actions: setEditingRowName(name)
    Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(ROW/EDIT_CHANGE, {name})
    Ctx->>Reducer: rows.editChange
    Reducer-->>Ctx: editingRowName = name
    Ctx-->>Row: editing RowSection's input re-renders<br/>(RowEditContext: editingRowName changed)

    User->>Row: Enter / blur
    Row->>Actions: saveRowTitle(rowId)
    Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(ROW/EDIT_SAVE, {rowId})
    Ctx->>Reducer: rows.editSave
    Reducer-->>Ctx: rows[rowId].title = trimmed (if non-empty)<br/>editingRowId = null
    Ctx-->>Row: that RowSection re-renders<br/>(BoardData: row.title changed)<br/>-> shows updated title
    Ctx-->>Row: every RowSection re-renders<br/>(RowEditContext: editingRowId=null)<br/>-> input reverts to text

    Note over Row: Escape → ROW/EDIT_CANCEL → rows.editCancel<br/>(discards edit, no title change.<br/>every RowSection re-renders via RowEditContext)

    Note over User,AI: Delete row (RowSection)
    User->>Row: click delete (confirm dialog)
    Row->>Actions: deleteRow(rowId)<br/>(actions/row.ts)
    Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(ROW/DELETE, {rowId})
    Ctx->>Reducer: rows.remove(state, payload)
    Reducer-->>Ctx: rows filtered. tasks for that row removed.<br/>clears any open modal/edit state referencing it
    Note over Reducer: Comments of the removed tasks are not deleted here:<br/>KV -> swept by the next /api/purge-trash run,<br/>localStorage -> pruned on the next board load
    Ctx-->>Row: that RowSection (+ its ColumnSections/TaskCards)<br/>unmounts (BoardData: rows/tasks changed)
    Ctx-->>Config: BoardConfiguration re-renders<br/>(BoardData: rows changed)<br/>-> row settings list loses the row
    Note over Ctx: Other tabs receive the new board via BOARD/SYNC<br/>(see board-load-autosave). If no rows are left there,<br/>their task modals close.

    Note over User,AI: Reorder row (move up / down, RowSettingsSection only)
    User->>Config: click move-up / move-down arrow
    Config->>Actions: moveRowUp(index) / moveRowDown(index)<br/>(actions/row.ts)
    Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(ROW/MOVE, {fromIndex, toIndex})
    Ctx->>Reducer: rows.move(state, payload)
    Reducer-->>Ctx: rows array reordered.<br/>moved row's order = generateKeyBetween(prev, next)
    Ctx-->>Config: BoardConfiguration re-renders<br/>(BoardData: rows reordered)<br/>-> row settings list shows new order
    Ctx-->>Row: RowSection instances re-render in new order<br/>(BoardData: rows reordered)<br/>-> RowBoard re-maps them by row.id

    Note over User,AI: Update row color (RowSettingsSection)
    User->>Config: change row color select
    Config->>Actions: updateRowColor(rowId, color)<br/>(actions/row.ts)
    Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(ROW/UPDATE_COLOR, {rowId, color})
    Ctx->>Reducer: rows.updateColor
    Reducer-->>Ctx: rows[rowId].color = color
    Ctx-->>Row: that RowSection re-renders<br/>(BoardData: row.color changed)<br/>-> background color-mix updates
    Ctx-->>Cell: every ColumnSection in that row re-renders<br/>(BoardData: row.color changed)<br/>-> background/border + add-task button tint update

    Note over Config: The Trash column is left out of the settings badge list,<br/>ColumnReorderList and the add-column reference select,<br/>so it cannot be renamed, deleted or moved, and stays last.<br/>Adding "right of" the last column, or dropping on the trailing<br/>drop zone, places the column before Trash
    Note over User,AI: Add column (ColumnSettingsSection, "Create a new column" form)
    User->>Config: type column name<br/>(defaultColumnInput)
    Config->>Actions: setDefaultColumnInput(value)<br/>(actions/columnConfig.ts)
    Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(COLUMN/SET_INPUT, {value})
    Ctx->>Reducer: columns.setInput
    Reducer-->>Ctx: defaultColumnInput = value
    Ctx-->>Config: BoardConfiguration re-renders<br/>(ColumnConfigContext: defaultColumnInput changed)

    User->>Config: pick direction (left/right) +<br/>reference column from the two selects
    Note over Config: direction + referenceColumnId are local<br/>component useState — no dispatch

    User->>Config: click "Add Column" (form submit)
    Note over Config: native form validation (required name + both selects)<br/>blocks submit until all fields are filled
    Config->>Actions: addColumn(direction, referenceColumnId)<br/>(actions/columnConfig.ts)
    Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(COLUMN/ADD, {id, title, order: end, icon: null})
    Ctx->>Reducer: columns.add(state, payload)
    Reducer-->>Ctx: columns = [...columns, newColumn]
    Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(COLUMN/REORDER, {columnId: id,<br/>beforeColumnId: left ? referenceId : column after reference})
    Ctx->>Reducer: columns.reorder
    Reducer-->>Ctx: new column spliced to chosen array index,<br/>order regenerated via generateKeyBetween(prev, next)
    Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(COLUMN/SET_INPUT, {value: ""})
    Ctx->>Reducer: columns.setInput
    Reducer-->>Ctx: defaultColumnInput = ""
    Config->>Config: reset local direction + referenceColumnId to ""
    Ctx-->>Config: BoardConfiguration re-renders<br/>(BoardData: columns changed)<br/>-> reference select lists the new column, name input clears
    Ctx-->>Cell: every RowSection mounts a new ColumnSection<br/>(BoardData: columns changed)<br/>-> appears to the left/right of the reference column

    Note over User,AI: Rename column (per ColumnSection, double-click)
    Note over Cell: The Trash column (isTrash) has no double-click rename<br/>and no "+" button. It shows a "deleted after 30 days" disclaimer
    User->>Cell: double-click column title
    Cell->>Actions: editColumnTitle(column, row)<br/>(actions/columnEdit.ts)
    Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(COLUMN/RENAME_START, {columnId, rowId, currentName})
    Ctx->>Reducer: columns.renameStart
    Reducer-->>Ctx: editingColumnId, editingColumnRowId, editingColumnName set
    Ctx-->>Cell: the matching ColumnSection (columnId, rowId)<br/>re-renders (ColumnEditContext changed)<br/>-> shows input

    User->>Cell: type name, Enter / blur
    Cell->>Actions: setEditingColumnName(name) -> saveColumnTitle(columnId)
    Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(COLUMN/RENAME_CHANGE, {name})<br/>dispatch(COLUMN/RENAME_SAVE, {columnId})
    Ctx->>Reducer: columns.renameChange / renameSave
    Reducer-->>Ctx: columns[columnId].title = trimmed (if non-empty)<br/>editingColumnId/editingColumnRowId = null
    Ctx-->>Cell: every ColumnSection for this column<br/>(across all rows) re-renders<br/>(BoardData: column.title changed)<br/>-> shows new title
    Ctx-->>Cell: the editing ColumnSection re-renders<br/>(ColumnEditContext: editingColumnId=null)<br/>-> input reverts to text

    Note over Cell: Escape → COLUMN/RENAME_CANCEL → columns.renameCancel<br/>(editing ColumnSection re-renders via ColumnEditContext,<br/>no title change)

    Note over User,AI: Delete column (ColumnSettingsSection)
    User->>Config: click delete on column badge
    Config->>Actions: deleteColumn(columnId)<br/>(actions/columnConfig.ts)
    Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(COLUMN/DELETE, {columnId})
    Ctx->>Reducer: columns.remove(state, payload)
    Reducer-->>Ctx: columns filtered. tasks for that column removed.<br/>clears any open modal/edit state referencing it
    Note over Reducer: Comments of the removed tasks are not deleted here:<br/>KV -> swept by the next /api/purge-trash run,<br/>localStorage -> pruned on the next board load
    Ctx-->>Config: BoardConfiguration re-renders<br/>(BoardData: columns changed)<br/>-> column settings badge list loses the column
    Ctx-->>Cell: the corresponding ColumnSection instance in<br/>every RowSection unmounts<br/>(BoardData: columns/tasks changed)

    Note over User,AI: Pin/unpin column — two independent menus:<br/>Shortcut Menu (#board-menu, lg+, max 3) and<br/>Dock Menu (BoardDock, below lg, max 1).<br/>Each has its own pin button in ColumnSettingsSection.
    alt Shortcut Menu pin
        User->>Config: click Shortcut Menu pin icon
        Config->>Actions: togglePinShortcut(columnId)<br/>(actions/columnConfig.ts)
        Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(COLUMN/TOGGLE_PIN_SHORTCUT, {columnId})
        Ctx->>Reducer: columns.togglePinShortcut(state, payload)
        Reducer-->>Ctx: columns[columnId].pinnedToShortcut = !pinnedToShortcut
        Ctx-->>BoardMenu: BoardView re-renders<br/>(BoardData: columns changed)<br/>-> #board-menu adds/removes that column's<br/>title+count item (lg+ only)
    else Dock Menu pin (max 1)
        User->>Config: click Dock Menu pin icon
        Config->>Actions: togglePinDock(columnId)<br/>(actions/columnConfig.ts)
        Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(COLUMN/TOGGLE_PIN_DOCK, {columnId})
        Ctx->>Reducer: columns.togglePinDock(state, payload)
        Reducer-->>Ctx: columns[columnId].pinnedToDock = !pinnedToDock
        Ctx-->>BoardMenu: BoardView re-renders<br/>(BoardData: columns changed)<br/>-> BoardDock shows/clears its single<br/>dock-pinned column item (below lg only)
    end
    Ctx-->>Config: BoardConfiguration re-renders<br/>(BoardData: column pin flags changed)<br/>-> pin icons + N/3 and N/1 counters update
    Note over Reducer: Unpinning from either menu prunes the column<br/>from selectedColumnIds only if it is no longer pinned<br/>to the other menu, so the view filter never references<br/>a column absent from both menus.

    Note over User,AI: Filter board by pinned column<br/>(shared view filter — Shortcut Menu item or Dock Menu item)
    User->>BoardMenu: click a pinned column item<br/>(#board-menu at lg+, or dock below lg)
    BoardMenu->>Actions: toggleColumnFilter(columnId)<br/>(actions/view.ts)
    Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(VIEW/TOGGLE_COLUMN_FILTER, {columnId})
    Ctx->>Reducer: view.toggleColumnFilter(state, payload)
    Reducer-->>Ctx: selectedColumnIds toggles the id<br/>(add if absent, remove if present)
    Ctx-->>BoardMenu: BoardMenu + BoardDock re-render<br/>(ColumnFilterContext: selectedColumnIds changed)<br/>-> selected items get the active state<br/>(bg-base-content/10 in menu, dock-active in dock)
    Ctx-->>Board: RowBoard re-renders<br/>(ColumnFilterContext: selectedColumnIds changed)
    alt 0 selected
        Board->>Row: render every RowSection with all columns
    else >=2 selected
        Board->>Row: render every RowSection;<br/>RowSection filters columns to selectedColumnIds
        Row->>Cell: ColumnSections only for selected columns
    else exactly 1 selected
        Board->>Board: render CondensedColumnBoard<br/>(CondensedColumnBoard.tsx)<br/>-> single section titled with the column;<br/>each row pivots into a horizontal ColumnSection<br/>(column fixed, headerLabel = row.title)
        Note over Cell: open/edit (TASK/OPEN_EDIT_MODAL) and drag<br/>reuse existing ColumnSection logic; dragging a task<br/>to another project column dispatches<br/>TASK/DROP_ON_CELL {toRowId, toColId: this column}
    end
    Note over Reducer: COLUMN/DELETE also prunes selectedColumnIds<br/>(columns.remove). selectedColumnIds is ephemeral —<br/>excluded from the autosave snapshot.

    Note over User,AI: Toggle "Display on shortcut menu" (per-column card,<br/>only shown once a column is pinned. Controls only<br/>whether that column's icon renders in the menu item -<br/>the item itself stays/goes based on pinned alone)
    User->>Config: check/uncheck "Display on shortcut menu"
    Config->>Actions: toggleIconInBoardMenu(columnId)<br/>(actions/columnConfig.ts)
    Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(COLUMN/TOGGLE_ICON_IN_BOARD_MENU, {columnId})
    Ctx->>Reducer: columns.toggleIconInBoardMenu(state, payload)
    Reducer-->>Ctx: columns[columnId].iconInBoardMenu = !iconInBoardMenu
    Ctx-->>Config: BoardConfiguration re-renders<br/>(BoardData: column.iconInBoardMenu changed)<br/>-> checkbox toggles
    Ctx-->>BoardMenu: BoardView re-renders<br/>(BoardData: columns changed)<br/>-> that column's item shows/hides its icon in<br/>#board-menu and (if dock-pinned) BoardDock<br/>(title+count badge unaffected)

    Note over User,AI: Reorder column (drag, ColumnSettingsSection column badges.<br/>Drag scaffolding + drop zones live in the shared<br/>ColumnReorderList.tsx; same dispatches whether rendered<br/>by ColumnSettingsSection or the homepage DemoExperience)
    User->>Config: dragstart on column badge
    Config->>Actions: handleDefaultColumnDragStart(index)<br/>(actions/columnConfig.ts)
    Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(COLUMN/SET_DRAGGED_INDEX, {index})
    Ctx->>Reducer: columns.setDraggedIndex
    Reducer-->>Ctx: draggedDefaultIndex = index
    Ctx-->>Config: BoardConfiguration re-renders<br/>(ColumnConfigContext: draggedDefaultIndex set)<br/>-> dragged badge dims to opacity 0.4

    User->>Config: dragover badge
    Config->>Config: preventDefault()<br/>setDragHoverIndex(index) (local state)
    Note over Config: hover indicator line is local useState,<br/>not dispatched to BoardContext<br/>→ ColumnSettingsSection re-renders locally only

    User->>Config: drop on target badge
    Config->>Actions: handleDefaultColumnDrop(targetColumnId)<br/>(actions/columnConfig.ts)
    Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(COLUMN/REORDER, {columnId: draggedId, beforeColumnId: targetColumnId})
    Ctx->>Reducer: columns.reorder(state, payload)
    Reducer-->>Ctx: columns array reordered.<br/>moved column's order = generateKeyBetween(prev, next)
    Actions->>Ctx: dispatch(COLUMN/SET_DRAGGED_INDEX, {index: null})
    Ctx->>Reducer: columns.setDraggedIndex
    Reducer-->>Ctx: draggedDefaultIndex = null
    Ctx-->>Config: BoardConfiguration re-renders<br/>(BoardData: columns reordered.<br/>ColumnConfigContext: draggedDefaultIndex=null)<br/>-> column settings badges reorder, dim clears
    Ctx-->>Cell: ColumnSection instances in every RowSection<br/>re-render in new order<br/>(BoardData: columns reordered)

    Note over User,AI: Autosave (debounced, async)
    Ctx->>Ctx: useBoardPersistence: useEffect on rows/columns/tasks (500ms debounce)
    Ctx->>Ctx: PUT /api/board {rows, columns, tasks}<br/>(or localStorage if unauthenticated)

    Note over User,AI: Sync drawer row list (DrawerMenu.astro,<br/>an Astro server island rendered outside the React tree —<br/>see BoardController's document-click-delegation note above)
    Ctx->>Ctx: useDrawerRowMirror (effects/useDrawerRowMirror.ts):<br/>useEffect on rows (after boardLoaded, skipped when boardId === "demo")
    Ctx->>Ctx: rebuild #drawer-row-list DOM via replaceChildren<br/>(li/a[data-board-link] per row, sorted by order)
    Note over Ctx: Runs on ROW/ADD, ROW/DELETE, ROW/EDIT_SAVE, ROW/MOVE —<br/>any change to state.rows. New anchors are picked up by<br/>BoardController's existing document click-delegation,<br/>so they still route through the SPA router.<br/>Skipped entirely for the homepage DemoExperience's<br/>BoardProvider (boardId === "demo"), whose rows are never<br/>the visitor's real rows and must not overwrite the shared<br/>#drawer-row-list.
